      "tail_model": "Each draw's true-setting IC is converted to a tail probability under the uniform-letter null (chi-square with 25 degrees of freedom, Wilson-Hilferty), multiplied by ranked_population to give the expected number of wrong keys above it, and the chance that fewer than `retained` of them outrank it is Poisson. The empirical null mean and sd are recorded beside the analytic ones so the model can be checked cell by cell; empirical exceedance has a resolution of one null trial and cannot reach the tail the ranking uses."
